first and then the site and checks.\n- MkDocs Material was chosen as the generator without a product-level review.\n\nOutput: [.ard/178/triage-engineer.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/bc8a1344fd2965089ec04406063152e40ddef7ee/.ard/178/triage-engineer.md) · log [.ard/178/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T122948.480Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/bc8a1344fd2965089ec04406063152e40ddef7ee/.ard/178/logs/triage-engineer-20261124T122948.480Z.log) · job `01M86RH86ZNGHDGKATS70GD43Y` · attempt 1\n\n\n# Plan for #178\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\nDecisions: generator is **MkDocs Material** (nav, search and `mkdocs build --strict` link checking come built in; Hugo and Jekyll need more custom work for the same result). Pages live in `docs/site/`; `mkdocs.yml` is new at the repo root with `docs_dir: docs/site`. `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/layout.md` and `docs/TODO.md` stay outside the site and user pages link to the proposal by absolute GitHub URL (strict mode rejects links leaving `docs_dir`). The Gate 2 runbook is copied-by-move into the site (step 4).\n\n1. **Config key source of truth (new, `internal/config/keys.go`).** Add `func Keys() []string` returning every documented dotted key: the top-level keys, `intervals.*`, `intake.mode|label`, `merge.protected_paths`, `stale.*`, `redact.gitleaks.*`, `sidecars.<name>.repo|ref`, and the override keys (`every`, `max_open`, `group_size`, `autoclose`, `route`, `model`, `timeout`, `sidecar`, `after`, `plan_section`, `tests`, `max_test_fixes`, `max_review_rounds`, `reviewers`, `diff_warn_lines`, `diff_max_lines`, `agent`). Derive from the `yaml:` tags of `resolvedYAML` and `roleYAML` in `internal/config/render.go` by reflection, and add the input-only keys (`merge.protected_paths`, `overrides`) from the list parsed in `internal/config/raw.go`. Add `keys_test.go` that fails if a key parsed in `raw.go` is missing from `Keys()` (so the list cannot lag the loader). Reason: the docs check needs one list that trac