{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014RPah1JSHbEFq6sUUrQUh7","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/proposal.md:511:Start on one repo (albertcbrown/ard itself, dogfooding; decided, #6) with the local executor and a human approval gate; humans merge until Gate 2, then the merger takes over. Widen only when the numbers say the loop is trustworthy. Gate 2 is run from [docs/runbooks/gate-2.md](runbooks/gate-2.md).\n# Layout\n\nEvery top-level directory and Go package, with what it holds. Keep it current: a PR that adds, removes or renames a directory or package updates this file in the same PR.\n\n```\ncmd/ard/                    CLI entry point; wire a new subcommand by adding one line to handlers()\ninternal/cli/               cobra command tree, global flags, slog logging; Handlers is the plug-in point\ninternal/botcheck/          tests for the bot-commit audit in .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\ninternal/github/            GitHub client: domain types, Reader/Writer/Client, App auth, retry transport; query/ (search builder), fake/ (test double), clienttest/ (conformance suite)\ninternal/config/            .ard/config.yaml + role directory loading into a Resolved value (pure, fs.FS in)\ninternal/configcmd/         `ard config check` handler: prints the resolved config, returns validation errors; `--ref` checks a commit\ninternal/configsrc/         config from origin/main: a snapshot per SHA under ~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/ (what `ard serve` reads)\ninternal/executor/          Executor interface and plain-data job types\ninternal/executor/local/    git worktree + host subprocess or docker run, watchdog, logs\ninternal/agent/             Adapter interface, Spec/Result types, Registry (pure: builds argv, parses output)\ninternal/agent/claude/      Claude Code adapter (`claude -p`, stream-json parser)\ninternal/modelauth/         picks the one model credential (OAuth token or API key) from the controller env and carries its value to the executor; never logged\ninternal/state/             SQLite controller and scanner state (sqlitex, scannerdb)\ninternal/scanner/           scanner pipeline: findings, markers, reconcile, diff, group, ExecEngine, the scanners Loop, rebuild\ninternal/costblock/         the issue body's ard-owned cost block: render, strict parse, strip (admission), splice, per-issue Locks; leaf, stdlib only\ninternal/costs/             the costs Loop: writes each dirty issue's cost table from state; Claims() false so it runs while paused\ninternal/scanner/stale/     the stale closer: a plain controller Loop that comments and closes untouched scanner issues\ninternal/agentjob/          helpers the agent loops share: untrusted-input snapshot, admission re-check, agent command and executor job builders, handle save, shutdown-aware wait, post-once\ninternal/worker/            the worker loop: claim, agent/test/fix steps, diff guard, code-lane push, draft PR, FinishWith\ninternal/servecmd/          `ard serve` and `ard rebuild-state`: dependency wiring (lock, state, effects, pool adoption, controller); registerLoops takes one line per loop\ninternal/redact/            log redaction (secrets and host paths), secret scan and 1 MiB cap (leaf library; close-out commits only LogResult.Clean)\ninternal/roles/             starter .ard/ tree (config.yaml, role dirs) embedded for ard init (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/lint, scanners/missing-tests, scanners/trufflehog, scanners/trufflehog-history, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review, reviewers/security-review)\ninternal/pool/              slot arbiter for max_pods (stdlib only, no I/O): priority classes, per-issue triage cap\ninternal/effects/           the only writer: Effects interface, Live and DryRun (JSONL ledger), Open factory; archtest/ enforces \"only effects writes\"\ninternal/gitx/              git CLI wrapper (Commit, Push, StagedPaths, FileAt); gittest/ builds bare-repo fixtures; Commit/Push are for internal/effects only\ninternal/wtlock/            serialises git worktree add/remove/prune per repository within the process (git worktree bookkeeping is not concurrency-safe, #109); leaf\ninternal/controller/        scheduler, kill switch (pause), leader lock, status issue\ninternal/committer/         the only commit/push path: .ard/<issue#>/ (main lane, per-branch lanes) and worker code on worker/ branches (CommitCode, CheckCodePath)\ninternal/closeout/          job close-out: role file or failure cause -> labels, comment, commits (resumable); per-role write allowlist (WritableFor); every job ends through its Closer\ninternal/reaper/            the Reaper loop (failed-job detection, retention, :running with no record) and reaper.Finisher, the end-of-job path the loops and the Reaper share\ninternal/limits/            the book of exhausted usage limits the pool consults (the reactive half; #63 adds readings and thresholds)\ninternal/budget/            the daily dollar-cap gate the pool consults (budget.Gate: role and repo caps from step_usage, UTC day, fails closed)\ninternal/intake/            intake admission: Admit decides whether a human-filed issue may enter triage (pure; the triage loop calls it)\ninternal/prgate/            reviews-passed-at-head decision shared by the reviewer's mark-ready and the merger: label rule, head Covers, reviewed heads, ParseWorkerBranch\ninternal/janitor/           the janitor loop: prunes .ard/<issue#>/ of issues closed over 90 days ago through the main committer; no slot\n# ard — automated repository development\n\nard makes a GitHub repository maintain itself. Scanners file deduplicated issues, triage agents turn each issue into a plan, a worker agent implements it on a branch, reviewer agents critique the PR, and a merger lands it once every review passes.\n\n> **Status:** design stage. Nothing runs yet. The design lives in [docs/proposal.md](docs/proposal.md), and the work is tracked as [GitHub issues](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues) grouped into phase milestones.\n\n## How it works\n\nOne rule holds the system together: **a deterministic controller owns every GitHub and git side effect; agents only read and write files in a worktree.**\n\nOne `ard` process per repository runs six loops that share a small pool of job slots (default 3):\n\n| Loop | Every | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Scanners | 4 h | Find problems (CVEs, outdated components, lint, docs, missing tests…), file or update issues, close what is fixed |\n| Triage | 15 min | Role agents (lead, PM, architect, designer, doc planner, engineer) turn an issue into `plan.md` |\n| Workers | 5 min | Implement the plan on `worker/<role>-<issue#>-<slug>`, run tests, open a draft PR |\n| Reviewers | 5 min | Role agents (security, license, eng, PM) review the PR and request fixes |\n| Merger | 5 min | Squash-merge PRs whose reviews all passed and whose checks are green |\n| Reaper | 1 min | Mark dead or overdue jobs `ard:executor:failed`, keep their evidence 24 h |\n\nGitHub labels prefixed `ard:` are the queue and the state machine. `.ard/<issue#>/` in the target repository holds each issue's plan, per-role summaries and full agent logs.\n\n## Configuration by convention\n\nA target repository opts in with an `.ard/` directory. A role exists because its directory exists:\n\n```\n.ard/\n├── config.yaml          # global settings and overrides only\nbot-commits.yml\nci.yml\nversion.yml\ninternal/initcmd:\nbody.go\ninitcmd.go\ninitcmd_test.go\nplan.go\n\ninternal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\ndocs_docker_integration_test.go\ndocs_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.go\nerrcodes_integration_test.go\nerrcodes_test.go\nlead_test.go\nlicense_review_integration_test.go\nlicense_review_test.go\nlint_docker_integration_test.go\nlint_integration_test.go\nlint_scan_test.go\nlint_test.go\nmissing_tests_integration_test.go\nmissing_tests_test.go\npm_review_test.go\nreviewers\nroles.go\nroles_test.go\nscanner_guard_test.go\nscanners\nsecurity_review_test.go\ntestdata\ntriage\ntriage_roles_test.go\ntrufflehog_docker_integration_test.go\ntrufflehog_history_test.go\ntrufflehog_integration_test.go\ntrufflehog_test.go\nworker_engineer_test.go\nworkers\n518:    P3 --> P4[\"Phase 4: Docs and site<br/>user documentation<br/>GitHub Pages site\"]\n522:Phases 4 and 5 have no gate: Phase 4 ([#178](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/178)) writes the user documentation and publishes it as a GitHub Pages site, and Phase 5 ([#177](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/177)) publishes versioned releases and a Homebrew cask (`brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`).\n# Gate 2 runbook: first loop proven (#39)\n\nGate 2 proves triage, worker and review on real issues before the merger takes\nover. ard runs live with the local executor on the owner's Mac, and a human\nmerges every PR. See [docs/proposal.md: Rollout](../proposal.md#rollout).\n\n**Done when** (from #39):\n\n- 10 PRs opened by ard are merged by a human\n- the executor failure rate is under 10% of agent jobs\n- the go/no-go for Phase 2 is recorded on #39, with the cost per merged PR\n\nTwo stages: a smoke run on `albertcbrown/ard-scratch` that walks one issue\nthrough every stage, then the gate itself on `albertcbrown/ard`.\n\n> **After the merger landed (#46).** `ard serve` now runs the merger loop, so it\n> squash-merges worker PRs that pass its gates and humans no longer merge them.\n> To keep human merging for this gate, start `serve` without it:\n> `ard serve --loops scanners,stale,triage,workers,reviewers,reaper`. A repo\n> without rulesets (the private free-plan `ard-scratch`) merges on reviews alone\n> after a two-minute grace period when the head has no check runs; with check\n> runs, all must be green. Run `ard serve --dry-run` first to read the\n> `merge.would_merge` lines. The merger's end-to-end test\n> (`go test -tags integration ./internal/merger`, `ARD_IT_REPO` set) also needs a\n> repo with rulesets plus CI for its red-check case (`ARD_IT_CI=1`): that case is\n> optional and skipped on `ard-scratch`.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n| What | Where |\n|---|---|\n| `ard` built from `main` | `make build`; record `./bin/ard version` (a behaviour change mid-gate is noted in the table) |\n| GitHub App `ard-bot-albertcbrown`, installed on both repos | contents, issues and pull requests read and write, checks read and write, no `workflows` (#85) |\n| App key | `~/.ard/keys/ard-scratch.pem`, mode 0600; 1Password ClaviumLabs / \"ard-scratch GitHub App\" |\n| Model credential | subscription OAuth token, 1Password Private / \"claude setup-token\" (`claude setup-token`) |\n| Extra usage off in the Claude account | otherwise a usage-limit stop may be billed as overage |\n| Host tools | `claude` at `TestedVersion`, `git`, `go`, `make`, Docker running (the cve scanner has a Dockerfile), `osv-scanner`, `govulncheck`, `jq`, `sqlite3` |\n\nEvery agent role without a `Dockerfile` runs as a host subprocess and logs the\n`executor.host_untrusted` warning (#84). That is expected on owner-controlled\ninternal/labels/catalogue.go:24:\t// Intake is the configured intake.label; \"\" = the default (ard:pending,\ninternal/labels/catalogue.go:90:\t\t\t\t\tcontinue // the lead's request is the static ard:pending\ninternal/labels/colors.go:10:\t\tStateRequest: {\"1d76db\", \"ard: triage %s requested\"},\ninternal/labels/colors.go:11:\t\tStateRunning: {\"0b4a8f\", \"ard: triage %s running\"},\ninternal/labels/colors.go:12:\t\tStateDone:    {\"c5def5\", \"ard: triage %s done\"},\ninternal/labels/colors.go:15:\t\tStateRequest: {\"5319e7\", \"ard: worker %s requested\"},\ninternal/labels/colors.go:16:\t\tStateRunning: {\"3b0f9e\", \"ard: worker %s running\"},\ninternal/labels/colors.go:17:\t\tStateDone:    {\"d4c5f9\", \"ard: worker %s done\"},\ninternal/labels/colors.go:20:\t\tStateRequest: {\"0e8a1