{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFFGNFpdLSimCJKcMVatdQ","type":"tool_result","content":"(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\n# Detective control for the main-lane committer (docs/proposal.md, \"The .ard/\n# contract\"). The bot bypasses branch protection on main, so this audits the\n# first-parent history of main and fails when a commit made by the bot changes\n# anything except regular files under a single .ard/<issue#>/ directory.\n#\n# The bot login and the optional baseline come from repository variables, which\n# the GitHub App cannot write. The App also lacks the `workflows` permission,\n# so it cannot edit this file. Both are why the logic is inline bash here and\n# not Go. internal/botcheck extracts the script below and tests it.\nname: ard bot commits\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  # Main-lane bot pushes carry [skip ci], which suppresses the push trigger, so\n  # a schedule is what catches a stretch of history made only of bot commits.\n  schedule:\n    - cron: '17 * * * *'\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  check:\ninternal/closeout/allow.go:21:// WritableFor returns the write allowlist of a job. n must already be\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-22-// positive (Prepare passes the dry-run-adjusted number). section is the\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-23-// plan.md heading the role owns (config.Role.PlanSection); it is granted only\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-24-// to triage roles.\ninternal/closeout/allow.go:25:func WritableFor(n int, stage, role, section string) Writable {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-26-\tw := Writable{RoleFile: agent.RoleFilePath(n, stage, role)}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-27-\tif stage != StageTriage {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-28-\t\treturn w\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-29-\t}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-30-\tw.Section = section\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-31-\tif role == \"designer\" {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-32-\t\tw.Prefixes = []string{fmt.Sprintf(\".ard/%d/design/\", n)}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-33-\t}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-34-\treturn w\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-35-}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-36-\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-37-// sectionOf finds the plan.md section of a triage role in the loaded config.\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-38-func sectionOf(rs RoleSet, stage, role string) string {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-39-\tif stage != StageTriage || rs == nil {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-40-\t\treturn \"\"\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-41-\t}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-42-\tr, ok := rs.Role(config.KindTriage, role)\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-43-\tif !ok {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-44-\t\treturn \"\"\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-45-\t}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-46-\treturn r.PlanSection\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-47-}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-48-\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-49-// checkWrites returns \"\" when every candidate is allowed, or a reason that\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-50-// names the first denied paths. Only a context error is returned as an error.\n--\ninternal/closeout/allow.go:52:\tw := WritableFor(n, j.Stage, j.Role, sectionOf(d.Roles, j.Stage, j.Role))\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-53-\tplanPath := fmt.Sprintf(\".ard/%d/plan.md\", n)\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-54-\tsorted := append([]candidate(nil), cands...)\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-55-\tsort.Slice(sorted, func(a, b int) bool { return sorted[a].path < sorted[b].path })\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-56-\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-57-\ttype denial struct{ path, why string }\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-58-\tvar denied []denial\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-59-\tfor _, c := range sorted {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-60-\t\tif err := ctx.Err(); err != nil {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-61-\t\t\treturn \"\", err\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-62-\t\t}\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-63-\t\tswitch {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-64-\t\tcase c.path == w.RoleFile:\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-65-\t\tcase underPrefix(c.path, w.Prefixes):\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-66-\t\tcase c.path == planPath && w.Section != \"\":\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-67-\t\t\tif c.delete {\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-68-\t\t\t\tdenied = append(denied, denial{c.path, \"deleted\"})\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-69-\t\t\t\tcontinue\ninternal/closeout/allow.go-70-\t\t\t}\n# ard configuration, proposed by `ard init`. Edit freely; this file is yours.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # Linter config a PR could weaken: disabling a linter silently autocloses its issues.\n    - \"**/.golangci.yml\"\n    - \"**/.golangci.yaml\"\ninternal/roles/reviewers:\neng-review\nlicense-review\nproduct-manager-review\nsecurity-review\n\ninternal/roles/scanners:\ncve\ndocs\nerror-codes\nlint\nmissing-tests\ntrufflehog\ntrufflehog-history\n\ninternal/roles/triage:\narchitect\ndesigner\ndocumentation-planner\nengineer\nlead\nproduct-manager\n\ninternal/roles/workers:\nengineer\nprompt.txt","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01e4fc37-f8b3-4c2b-bf25-32591dc5b174","uuid":"38abbb07-5be9-420b-9273-0486f381abc4","timestamp":"2026-11-2